    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Riverside was originally known as Dogget and served as a shipping center for copper mines in the Sierra Madre Mountain Range.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wyomingcarboncounty.com/blog/219-discover-riverside-wyoming-a-small-town-with-big-adventure"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Newton Doggett purchased the town of Riverside for only one dollar in 1900.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.riversidewyo.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Riverside is tied for the coldest inhabited spot in Wyoming, with a record low of minus sixty-six degrees Fahrenheit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverside%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The forty-room Riverside Hotel once served as a primary meeting place for miners flocking to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.riversidewyo.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Riverside has historically relied on agriculture and logging as its primary sources of income.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.riversidewyo.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Riverside sits along the banks of the Encampment River, making the area ideal for fishing, rafting, and kayaking.",
